    "updated_at": "2017-06-19T17:02:44Z",
    "body": "I looked at the first few.  I see:\r\n\r\n* https://www.bezeqint.net/bbl-log-1.0-SNAPSHOT/faq -- I get a 404, page has no dir attrs.\r\n* http://www.acoforum.org/uc/intro.html -- `<html dir=\"l2r\">`; doesn't matter what unicode-bidi value is used here, I suspect.\r\n* http://timeinc-under-20.bannerflow.com/resources/custom-resource-410bec79-ded3-44d7-841a-00ef6e225de6.html?cb=636293162136339001 -- `dir = dir || 'next'` false positive in inline JS.\r\n* http://timeinc-under-20.bannerflow.com/resources/custom-resource-410bec79-ded3-44d7-841a-00ef6e225de6.html?cb=636293162136339001 -- same thing.\r\n* https://policy.cookieinformation.com/05e08061-c8c5-440e-ace4-fe83754de9ec/cc.js?renew=false&referer=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.sikkertrafik.dk&culture=da&dnt=false&forceshow=false&cbid=05e08061-c8c5-440e-ace4-fe83754de9ec&whitelabel=true&brandid=CookieConsent -- false-positive; it's a JS file but has a query string so failed the `RIGHT(url, 3) != \".js\"` filter.  Lots of those in the list, actually.\r\n* https://www.gayroyal.com/framed/menu.asp -- `<img dir=\"Up\">` and same with \"Down\".  unicode-bidi value doesn't seem relevant.\r\n* https://inffuse-fbpopup.appspot.com/widget.html?cacheKiller=1495341596035&compId=i1daflzh&deviceType=desktop&height=40&instance=kX3fEmUDstGIz_ozKLWkYvKoOMAihvN3hA1aVNgUsSc.&locale=en&pageId=masterPage&viewMode=site&vsi=f3c5a6d0-7fee-4328-986b-b005137ffb32&width=205 -- `<div dir=\"[[fbpage.direction]]\">` which presumably gets replaced by a valid value when the widget is instantiated.\r\n* http://www.al-jazirah.com/2017/20170516/most.xml -- not HTML; some sort of XML data with `<news_capsules dir=\"/2017/20170516/\">`.\r\n* https://www.expatads.com/images/SocialButtons/google.png -- total noise.  ;)\r\n* http://cookies-consent.skoda-auto.com/dialogues/ImplicitConsent?culture=sk-SK -- `<html dir=&quot;ltr&quot;` (yes, with the entity escapes).  Doesn't matter what unicode-bidi is on the root element anyway.\r\n\r\nFiltering out the various `.js?stuff` bits from the list would probably cut it down a good bit.",
