    "updated_at": "2017-06-20T10:48:38Z",
    "body": "I figure it is more likely to make a difference for pages that in right-to-left languages, since they're more likely to mix directions. Checking https://www.w3.org/International/questions/qa-scripts#directions plus https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Internet_top-level_domains#Country_code_top-level_domains is a starting point for which URLs to check in the list...\r\n\r\nIn devtools, this selector can be used to find a relevant element:\r\n```\r\n[dir]:not([dir=ltr]):not([dir=rtl]):not([dir=auto]):not(:root)\r\n```\r\n\r\nI noticed that netflix had `dir=\"false\"` on a div, so I checked the [arabic version of netflix](https://netflix.com/ar), but it would just redirect based on my IP (I don't have a VPN available where right-to-left language is prevalent)...\r\n\r\nhttp://www.aop.gov.af/ has \r\n```\r\n<span class=\"posted\" dir=\"‘rtl’\">\r\n<table>\r\n<tbody><tr>\r\n<td>1396 </td>\r\n<td>جوزا </td>\r\n<td>28</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n</span>\r\n```\r\nbut doesn't render differently by adding `style=\"unicode-bidi: inherit\"` as far as I can tell.",
