    "created_at": "2017-10-09T15:20:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-09T15:20:46Z",
    "body": "I may need to give it some more thought, and i'm open to counter arguments, but my first reaction would be that we should set isolation, since it is applied for all correct `dir` attribute values, and presumably the folks using incorrect values are trying to produce a `dir`-like effect. Associating `dir` with isolation solves a lot of long-standing problems for folks working with bidi text.\r\n\r\n(Btw, fwiw, note that we were hoping that Safari would support isolation for `dir` by now, since they already support isolation in CSS - see https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=171761)\r\n\r\n(Edge hasn't yet got to grips with isolation, which is a disappointment, but occasionally exhibits some isolating behaviour in code that is older than HTML5. Fwiw, there are some tests for `dir `isolation at https://www.w3.org/International/tests/repo/results/the-dir-attribute-isolation)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
